Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 1 — Java-Based Android Applications (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn the complete methodology for understanding a traditional Java-based Android application. This roadmap focuses on reconstructing architecture, execution flow, framework interaction, and runtime behavior from the APK. It assumes you already have the foundational knowledge from the general reverse engineering methodology and now want a Java-specific workflow.



> Core Principle:
Java APKs are object-oriented systems built around the Android Framework. Recover the architecture first, then the implementation.




