Stage 31 — Common Java APK Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Reading classes alphabetically.

Ignoring the Android framework lifecycle.

Treating package names as architecture.

Spending excessive time on generated code.

Following utility classes before understanding features.

Ignoring object ownership and state.

Assuming decompiled Java perfectly matches original source.



---

Stage 32 — Java APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify and profile a Java-based Android application.

✅ Recover its architecture, package structure, and major subsystems.

✅ Reconstruct lifecycle-driven execution and framework interactions.

✅ Build call graphs, control-flow graphs, and data-flow models for Java code.

✅ Trace objects, state, collections, Intents, and persistence through the application.

✅ Distinguish handwritten business logic from generated and framework code.

✅ Correlate static analysis with runtime observations.

✅ Produce comprehensive, evidence-based documentation explaining the application's architecture and behavior.



